# Line endings are part of the claim this repository makes.
#
# The contract's bytes are hashed, deployed, and compared against the chain, so
# a working copy that quietly swaps LF for CRLF produces a file that hashes
# differently on one machine than another -- and "byte-identical to the deployed
# bytes" stops meaning anything the moment it depends on who checked it out.
#
# So every text file is LF in the working tree on every platform, not only in
# the object store.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary
